From f53b854025da7cca8e116e27c7c38bea802228ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:33:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Core][MoE] Make the grouped-expert fan-out measurable

The step anatomy spends 148 us per layer-step on grouped expert kernels and each
distinct expert costs 4.92 MB of fp8 weight traffic, so achieved bandwidth is the
distinct count times 33.2 GB/s. Twenty reads as 665 GB/s against the 895 the dense
path sustains in the same step, which leaves up to 1.4x on 27% of the step; 27 or
more puts the kernels at the ceiling and closes the axis. The existing "~20" in
results.md was inferred from the kernel time and then quoted back to excuse it, so
it proves nothing either way and the question needs measuring.

Upstream's own routing return cannot answer it: vllm/config/vllm.py:1201 refuses
--enable-return-routed-experts at pipeline_parallel_size > 1. VLLM_MOE_FANOUT_PROBE=1
hooks the shared router instead and works at PP=4 on the real lane. Three
constraints were checked in code first. Humming experts derive from
FusedMoEExpertsModular, so is_monolithic() is False and the production path goes
through select_experts rather than the monolithic branch that bypasses it. The
counting read synchronises, so only one forward in 32 is measured. And nothing is
measured while a CUDA graph is captured.

Decode forwards are themselves captured, so at replay no Python runs and they are
invisible apart from dummy ids at capture time. Prefill forwards do run in Python
and a forward of many rows contains many groups of STEP_ROWS adjacent tokens, which
is the same quantity, the distinct experts one step of that many rows must read. So
large forwards contribute the union over every sliding window of five adjacent rows
in the first 128, small forwards are counted whole, and capture-time calls are
skipped.

The hook reports counts only: no model geometry and no kernel timing lives here,
and benchmark/expert_fanout_probe.py does the arithmetic. It also writes a startup
proof once per worker, because an absent patch and an unset variable otherwise look
identical. 8 CPU tests, ruff and mypy clean.
